          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Almost always because the deck is too short and you are subconsciously shortening your stride to stay clear of the rear roller. That produces a choppier gait with more calf work and less hip extension than your outdoor running, which is also why treadmill-specific calf and Achilles complaints are common. A 60-inch deck largely resolves it.",
